STYLE='Chunky 16-bit pixel art with big square pixels on a consistent grid, flat colors with 3-4 shades per material, solid dark purple-black 1-pixel outline (#1a1220), no gradients, no anti-aliasing, no texture noise. Palette: warm sunset oranges and peach, warm honey wood, red paper-lantern red, teal roof-tile accents, cream paper, dusty violet and plum shadows.'
P_PLAT="Game asset sheet for a cozy Japanese noodle-house tower climbing game at dusk. Transparent background, items widely separated by empty space, all items seen straight from the side (orthographic, no perspective), no text. LEFT two-thirds of the image: five long horizontal platform bars stacked top to bottom, each bar exactly the same size, about 6 times wider than tall, with big empty gaps between them: (1) a sturdy warm honey-orange wooden beam with a bright top edge, simple wood grain, bevelled wooden end caps and a darker brown underside; (2) a moving platform: the same wooden plank wrapped with two steel bands with rivets, steel end caps and tiny round wheels tucked under the ends; (3) a fragile platform: old pale cracked terracotta clay slab with a few bold cracks and chipped edges; (4) the same clay slab badly broken: big jagged cracks right through it, missing chunks, crumbling bits, darker; (5) a heavy lift block: dark red lacquered stone block with gold trim and two small iron chain rings on top. RIGHT third: two bouncy spring pads stacked vertically: (6) a small red-lacquered wooden pad on a steel coil spring, squashed down and compressed; (7) the same spring pad fully extended and tall. $STYLE"
P_PROPS="Game asset sheet for a cozy Japanese noodle-house tower climbing game at dusk: 9 separate items in a neat 3 by 3 grid, widely separated by empty transparent space, each item centered in its cell, no text. Row 1: (1) a black crow flying to the RIGHT with wings raised high, yellow beak, white eye glint; (2) the same black crow flying to the right with wings swept down; (3) a single curved teal glazed Japanese roof tile, tumbling. Row 2: (4) dangerous hanging wind chimes: a short cord holding a cluster of sharp spiky steel rods and pointed spikes, clearly a hazard; (5) a bright golden dog biscuit shaped like a bone, very readable; (6) a bronze Japanese temple bell hanging inside a small red wooden frame with a little teal tiled roof. Row 3: (7) a puffy red zabuton floor cushion seen from the side, wide and flat, with small gold tassels at the corners; (8) a small bright gold triangular pennant flag with a red border on a thin wooden pole; (9) a simple bold paw-print icon, cream white with pink pads. Transparent background. $STYLE"
P_WALL="Seamless tileable pixel-art texture of a Japanese noodle-house tower facade, straight-on flat front view, orthographic, no perspective, no sky, fills the whole image edge to edge. One storey of the building: weathered wooden timber frame with horizontal beams and vertical posts, peach-cream plaster panels, two lit shoji paper windows glowing warm, a small red paper lantern hanging on a post, a narrow wooden ledge. The pattern must repeat seamlessly top-to-bottom and left-to-right. It is a BACKGROUND behind the gameplay, so use muted mid-tone colors with low contrast (dusty plaster, mid-brown wood, soft warm window glow), nothing very dark and nothing very bright. Pixel art on a coarse grid (about 192 pixels across), even lighting, no vignette, no text. $STYLE"
P_SKY="Distant city skyline silhouette at dusk for a parallax background, transparent background above the buildings. A wide row of distant Japanese town rooftops, a small pagoda, a temple roof, water towers and utility poles, two layered depths: far layer in dusty violet, nearer layer in deep plum, with a few tiny warm-lit windows. The silhouette is anchored to the bottom edge and fills the bottom half; the top half of the image is completely empty and transparent. No sky color, no sun, no text. $STYLE"
P_STREETROOF="Two separate wide horizontal building strips for a Japanese noodle-house tower game, on a transparent background, stacked with a big empty gap between them, each strip spans the full image width and is about 5 times wider than tall, straight-on flat front view, no perspective, no text or letters. TOP strip: the rooftop crown of the tower: a wide Japanese roof of teal glazed tiles with upturned eave corners and a flat wooden deck on top where a bell can stand, a red wooden railing, small gold ridge ornaments, transparent sky above. BOTTOM strip: the street-level shop front of the noodle house: dark wooden facade, a cream noren curtain hanging over the doorway in the center, a small wooden hanging sign with a bowl-of-noodles picture (no letters), two red paper lanterns, a sliding lattice window glowing warm, and a grey stone pavement strip along the very bottom. $STYLE"
P_PLAT_MED="Redraw this platform sprite sheet (reference image) cleanly at the same layout, positions and sizes: five long horizontal platform bars on the left, two spring pads on the right, transparent background, no text. Keep bars 1-4 as they are (honey wood beam; steel-banded wooden plank with small wheels; cracked pale terracotta slab; badly broken terracotta slab). Changes: bar 5 (lift block): keep the dark red lacquered block with gold trim, but replace the iron rings with two small BRIGHT GOLD rings with a clearly visible round hole, sitting flush on top near each end, rounded and friendly, nothing pointy. Springs: make both spring pads WIDE and LOW: a wide flat red-lacquered pad on top, a wide base plate at the bottom, short silver coils between: (6) compressed: very flat, about 3 times wider than tall; (7) extended: the same width, about 1.5 times wider than tall, coils stretched. Every bar has a bright highlight line along its top edge and a darker underside so the walkable top surface is obvious. $STYLE"
P_PROPS_MED="Redraw this 3 by 3 prop sprite sheet (reference image) cleanly in the same layout, positions and sizes, transparent background, no text. Keep: (1)(2) the two black crow frames, (4) the hanging spiky wind chimes but with brighter silver steel spikes and a red cord, (5) the golden dog-biscuit bone, (6) the bronze bell in the red wooden frame with teal roof, (7) the red zabuton cushion with gold tassels, (8) the gold pennant flag on a pole. Changes: (3) replace the rolled sheet with a single Japanese roof tile: a thick curved teal-glazed ceramic tile shaped like half of a short pipe, seen from the side at a tilt, darker teal underside, clearly a heavy roof tile; (9) make the paw print very simple and bold for a tiny icon: one big rounded pad and four round toe beans, cream white with a thick dark outline, light pink pad centres. $STYLE"
P_WALL_MED="Seamless tileable pixel-art texture of a Japanese noodle-house tower facade at dusk, straight-on flat front view, orthographic, fills the whole image edge to edge, no sky, no ground. This is a quiet BACKGROUND behind a platform game, so: dark-to-mid dusky colors, LOW contrast, muted and desaturated: plum-brown timber posts, dusty mauve-rose plaster panels, small shoji paper windows glowing soft amber, a few small red paper lanterns hanging on the posts. Strong VERTICAL rhythm: vertical posts and window columns. Horizontal beams are thin and flush with the wall. NO ledges, NO shelves, NO balconies, NO awnings, NO roof tiles, nothing that sticks out horizontally (those would be confused with platforms). The pattern must repeat seamlessly top-to-bottom and left-to-right: exactly 2 window bays across and exactly 3 storeys down. Chunky 16-bit pixel art on a coarse grid (about 192 pixels across), flat colors, 3 shades per material, no gradients, no noise, even lighting, no vignette, no text."
P_TITLE="Video game title logo that reads exactly \"SOBA TOWER\" (two words, all capitals, spelled S-O-B-A T-O-W-E-R) in big chunky blocky pixel-art lettering, 16-bit arcade style. Letters filled with a warm sunset gradient made of flat pixel bands (cream to orange to red), a thick dark purple-black outline (#1a1220) and a darker plum drop shadow. A small cute pixel-art head of the dog from the reference image (black fur, tall pointed ears with pink insides, tan eyebrow dots, white muzzle, pink tongue out) peeks over the top of the letter O in SOBA. One small red paper lantern hangs beside the word TOWER. The logo is centered and fills most of the frame on a perfectly flat, solid, pure green background (#00FF00) with nothing else on it: no gradient, no texture, no border, no other text."
